{"ts": "2026-10-17T13:35:25.454352Z", "run_id": "r-20261017T1320Z-5212", "unit": "openspec:add-telemetry-heavy-path-spans", "seq": 52, "type": "task.done", "task": "1.3", "base": "561c588882bcaf7dd1940824237cd90e7065403d", "parents": [], "notes": "Accepted findings: F-b98cfc - the search_phase failure half is covered here: C-20646f63 (a raising block marks the span ERROR with error.type and still records the phase point) and C-0d312d3f (a raising record_value is swallowed). The failing-embedder, ConversionError/VisionError outcome=failed, caught-CoChangeUnavailable outcome=unavailable and files.updated/.unchanged/.failed cases belong to tasks 3.x/4.x/5.x, not this task. F-8f538f concerns span(kind=...) typing (task 1.2) and is untouched here. Note on the person's retry note: the red tests enter the context and assert the handle is not None inside the block and that the span/point exists after, all satisfied. search_phase reuses the existing span() helper via a module-level alias (_span_context = span) because the boolean parameter shadows the span function name. test_search_phase_swallows_a_metric_recording_failure patches telemetry.record_value and the helper resolves it at call time, so the failure is caught. The failing-stage path lets span()'s SDK default also record an exception event; the runtime scrubber drops its message at export, which the privacy criteria rely on.", "suppressions": [{"file": "packages/core/src/mintmory/core/telemetry.py", "line": 835, "rule": "BLE001", "reason": "an attribute write on a span must never raise into the search caller"}, {"file": "packages/core/src/mintmory/core/telemetry.py", "line": 848, "rule": "BLE001", "reason": "a metric record must never raise into the search caller"}, {"file": "packages/core/src/mintmory/core/telemetry.py", "line": 892, "rule": "type: ignore[return-value]", "reason": "same wraps-based decorator pattern as traced(); the wrapper is Callable[..., Any]"}]}
